17. Bxe4 gxf4 18. Bxf4) 17. Ba3 d6 18. Re1+ Kf8 19. Kg2 Kg8 20. Ne6 Nbd7 21.
Nc7 (21. Bf5 {followed by Be6 and White has excellent chances (BCM). If} Ne5 (
21... Qh5 $17 {Stockfish 15}) 22. Bxc5) 21... Ne5 22. Rxe5 Qxc7 23. Re1 Qf7 24.
c4 Ng4 25. Qc2 Ne5 26. Rf1 $2 (26. Bxh7+ Kh8 27. Bb2 $11 {Stockfish 15}) 26...
Nxd3 27. Qxd3 Qh5 28. Rf4 Bh3+ 29. Kf2 Bg4 30. Kg1 Re8 31. Re4 Rf8 32. Re1 Bh3
33. Bb2 Qf7 34. Qe2 b5 35. cxb5 Qxd5 36. Ba1 Qf7 37. a4 d5 38. Be5 d4 {Source:
BCM, July 1947, p218. BCM gives the match date as 12 July but I'm convinced
this should be 12 June as it is the July issue of BCM and in all probability
this was a warm-up event for the GBR-CZE match that followed on 14-15 June. JS}
